/// GET/PUT /api/settings/event-notifications (admin, CSRF). Log retention, default quiet hours and
/// a list of notification rules: which events (kinds of data/events.json), to which targets (Home
/// Assistant notify actions such as the Companion app, Telegram or e-mail – they reach people with
/// the app closed – and/or paired devices, shown in the app while it is open; every paired device
/// except watches may be chosen, also children and guests), filtered by person, device, profile,
/// area, entity and route, with quiet hours, a threshold against spam and bundling. The hub sends
/// them itself (notify.<service> over its Home Assistant connection, devices through the hub
/// channel); the HA events <ns>_event and <ns>_alarm are always fired, independent of these
/// settings. PUT does not check notify targets against Home Assistant (it may be down); 422
/// notifications.no_target only for enabled rules without target, 422 notifications.device_unknown
/// for a device that is not paired, a watch or an expired guest, 422 notifications.duplicate_id. A
/// device that is deleted or whose guest access ends is removed from all rules (targets and
/// filters); a rule left without target is switched off. POST
/// /api/settings/event-notifications/test sends a test
/// (rest/event-notifications-test.request.json).
